; ==============================================================================
; aot_vs_interpret.lin
; ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Property:  AOT-compiled (.line binary container) runs the SAME net as the
;            interpreted source, with no optimizer between them.
;
;            A single source is already optimal-by-construction, so the AOT
;            build is a serialization + binary front-load step, NOT a
;            transformation: the .line container embeds the same compiled nets
;            that the interpreter would build (for a multi-form suite it keeps
;            the final net), and produces the same value as running that
;            expression directly.  There is no interpreter overhead to remove
;            and no optimizer to run.
;
;            This example is INTERACTIVE (no `; expect` lines => it is reported
;            but not value-checked).  It shows three equivalent ways to run the
;            program and lets you compare their `-b` (bench) step counts.
;
; How to run (all from the repo root):
;   # 1) Interpret the source directly:
;   ./lin examples/optimization/aot_vs_interpret.lin
;
;   # 2) AOT-compile to a .line binary container, then run it (the container
;   #     keeps the suite's final net, so its one printed value is the same as
;   #     that expression run on its own):
;   ./lin build examples/optimization/aot_vs_interpret.lin -o /tmp/aot.line
;   ./lin /tmp/aot.line
;   ./lin build /tmp/single.lin -o /tmp/single.line   # (single-form: identical)
;
;   # 3) Run either one under `-b` (bench: normalize the net, count reduction
;   #     steps).  `-b` is a measurement flag, NOT an optimizer:
;   ./lin -b examples/optimization/aot_vs_interpret.lin
;   ./lin -b /tmp/aot.line
;
;   The graph being normalized is the same optimal interaction net either way.
;   Extra passes are simply not part of the pipeline: source -> parser/normalizer
;   -> net is already optimal, and build .line just freezes the same nets into a
;   container.
; ==============================================================================
(load "std/std.lin")

; The same expression, several times, so both the interpreted and AOT runs have
; a comparable slice of work to report.
(mul (add 34 8) (sub 9 2))
(add 1 (add 2 (add 3 (add 4 5))))
(pow (add 2 1) 3)